                "description": "I joined Inertia to help shape the future of construction by unlocking the full potential of AI in the field. As CTO, I\u2019m focused on transforming how teams interact with project data\u2014turning static information into actionable intelligence that drives better decisions, faster execution, and safer outcomes.\n\nAfter decades building technology for the construction industry, I saw an opportunity at Inertia to solve one of its biggest challenges: turning overwhelming project data into something useful, accessible, and predictive. As CTO, I\u2019m helping lead that transformation with a deeply embedded AI strategy.\n\nOur mission is to embed AI into the core of project workflows, enabling automation of understanding, uncovering hidden risks and patterns, and empowering teams to act faster and with greater confidence\u2014from design through execution.\n\nCurrent Focus Areas:\n\n\u2022  AI-First Platform Architecture: Designing systems that interpret and connect plans, specs, RFIs, and field data into a dynamic, searchable system of record.\n\n\u2022 Intelligent Construction Agents: Building AI tools that identify risk, coordinate scope, and assist field teams in real time\u2014before issues escalate.\n\n\u2022 Human-Centered Interfaces: Creating intuitive visualizations that surface critical insights without adding noise\u2014bridging the gap between complexity and usability.\n\n\u2022 Industry-Driven Innovation: Collaborating closely with ENR contractors to ensure the platform delivers real-world impact and scales effectively across diverse projects.",
